#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:200
msgid "Shortest gap between two messages to one person"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:204
msgid "Counted across every basket, so somebody who abandons twice in an afternoon hears from you once."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:208
msgid "Most recovery attempts per person per month"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:211
msgid "A rolling thirty days, not a calendar month."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:217
msgid "Ignore baskets worth less than"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:220
msgid "In the shop currency. Zero chases every basket. Set this above the cost of a message if small baskets are not worth recovering."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:227
msgid "Quiet hours"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:228
msgid "Hours when nothing is sent. A message held back waits for the window to open rather than being dropped."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:231
msgid "Do not disturb"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:235
msgid "Hold messages overnight"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:236
msgid "A recovery message that arrives at three in the morning is remembered for the wrong reason."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:240
msgid "Quiet from"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:242
msgid "In this site's timezone, not the customer's. RecoveryFlow does not know where a phone number is being read."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:246
msgid "Quiet until"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:248
msgid "An end earlier than the start means the quiet window crosses midnight, which is the usual case."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:255
msgid "Recovery links"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:256
msgid "The link in a reminder that puts the basket back. The same link is what an unsubscribe uses, which is why its lifetime is a compliance setting as well as a convenience one."
