#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:312
msgid "WhatsApp"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:313
msgid "The channel RecoveryFlow is built around. Sending needs a connected WA.cr workspace."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:316
#: src/Core/Health.php:232
msgid "WhatsApp reminders"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:320
msgid "Send reminders over WhatsApp"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:321
msgid "Workflow steps set to WhatsApp are skipped while this is off. Nothing else changes: baskets are still recorded and journeys still run."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:329
msgid "A recovery email is commercial mail, and the law asks for two things before one may be sent: a real postal address for the business sending it, and an unsubscribe link that keeps working. RecoveryFlow refuses to send email until both are settled."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:332
msgid "Before email can be switched on"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:333
msgid "Settling all of these makes email reminders permissible. It does not switch them on -- that is still a separate decision, on the card below."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:338
msgid "Postal address of the business"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:341
msgid "One line per line, exactly as you would write it on an envelope. It is printed at the foot of every recovery email and is never translated or reformatted. A registered office or a post-office box is fine where the law of your country allows one."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:345
msgid "Country that address is in"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:346
msgid "Asked separately because an address is laid out according to its own country, and nothing in the text of an address reliably says which country it is in."
msgstr ""

