msgid "Auto Flow hook address"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:427
msgid "Copied from the Auto Flow in WA.cr that should pick these journeys up. Each request is signed, so a hook address on its own is not enough for anyone else to trigger your flow."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:431
msgid "Send from"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:433
msgid "The WhatsApp number in your workspace that reminders come from. Leave empty to use the workspace default."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:440
msgid "What is shared with WA.cr"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:441
msgid "A reminder cannot be sent without sending WA.cr the number it goes to. Everything beyond that is optional and off unless you turn it on."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:444
msgid "Optional details"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:448
msgid "Share the customer's last name"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:449
msgid "First names are shared because message templates usually greet somebody by one. Last names are not, unless a template you use needs one."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:453
msgid "Share the customer's email address"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:454
msgid "Only needed if your WA.cr workspace matches contacts by email or sends email itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:458
msgid "Honour opt-outs recorded in WA.cr"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:459
msgid "Somebody who replies STOP in WhatsApp is opted out in WA.cr. With this on, this site checks that before sending and stops messaging them too."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:476
msgid "Why this site may message somebody"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:477
msgid "The most consequential setting here. It decides who RecoveryFlow considers reachable, and it is the one a regulator would ask about first."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:480
msgid "Basis for messaging"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:484
msgid "Message somebody when"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:486
msgid "They ticked a box asking for reminders"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:487
msgid "They gave their details at the checkout"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:488
msgid "Never -- record baskets but message nobody"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:490
msgid "Asking first is the safe answer everywhere and the only defensible one in the EU and the UK. Treating a typed phone number as permission may be lawful where you trade; it is your decision and your risk, and RecoveryFlow records which basis each message was sent under either way."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:494
msgid "Wording of the consent tick-box"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:497
msgid "Send me a reminder if I do not finish my order"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:498
msgid "Shown at the checkout. Leave empty for the default wording. What was agreed to is stored with each consent, so changing this does not rewrite what anyone previously agreed to."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:505
msgid "How long anything is kept"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:506
msgid "An abandoned basket says what somebody was about to buy. There is no reason to still know that a year later, so finished journeys are stripped of their contents on a schedule."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:509
msgid "Retention"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:513
msgid "Keep the contents of a finished journey for"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:517
msgid "After this the basket contents, the notes and the session are removed and the amounts and dates stay, because those are your trading record rather than anything about a person. A week is the shortest this plugin will honour: shorter throws away the evidence you need when somebody asks why they were messaged, and that question always arrives late."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:524
msgid "Deleting the plugin"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:525
msgid "What happens to the data if RecoveryFlow is removed from this site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:528
msgid "On uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:532
msgid "Delete everything when the plugin is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:534
msgid "Off by default, because deactivating a plugin by accident is common and losing every consent record is not recoverable. With this on, deleting the plugin drops its tables -- including the record of who asked not to be messaged."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:535
msgid "This will delete every recovery record, including who opted out, when the plugin is deleted. Continue?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:552
msgid "Logging"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:553
msgid "RecoveryFlow keeps a short diagnostic log. Contact details, message contents and API keys are stripped out before anything is written, so the log says what happened without saying who it happened to."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:556
msgid "Diagnostic log"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:560
msgid "Record"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:562
msgid "Failures only"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:563
msgid "Failures and warnings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:564
msgid "Everything of note"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:565
msgid "Everything, for diagnosing a problem"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:567
msgid "Leave on failures and warnings for normal running. The most detailed setting writes a great deal on a busy shop; turn it back down once you have what you needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:571
msgid "Keep log entries for"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings/Schema.php:575
msgid "Older entries are removed by the daily clear-out."
msgstr ""

